THOUGHT: The error is about the constructor not guaranteeing initialization of the non-null field `region`. Since `region` is already initialized at declaration and the constructor delegates to `setRegion`, the issue is likely that NullAway thinks `setRegion` might set it to null. To satisfy NullAway without changing behavior, I’ll add a null-check in the `TextureRegionDrawable(TextureRegion region)` constructor to ensure `this.region` is always non-null, defaulting to a new `TextureRegion()` when the argument is null. Then I’ll run the Gradle compile to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '44,46c\  public TextureRegionDrawable(TextureRegion region) {
    if (region == null) {
      this.region = new TextureRegion();
    } else {
      setRegion(region);
    }
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/utils/TextureRegionDrawable.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "METHOD_NO_INIT" new_build_output.log | head || true
```

